      "message": {
        "content": "The Swiss Ice Hockey Federation (SIHF) is the governing body for ice hockey in Switzerland. It was founded on September 27, 1908, and is a founding member of the International Ice Hockey Federation (IIHF), which recognized it on November 23, 1908. The SIHF manages both amateur and professional ice hockey within Switzerland, including national teams at junior and senior levels.\n\n**Business Model:**\nThe SIHF operates as the overarching organization for Swiss ice hockey. Its business model revolves around overseeing and developing the sport through several key sectors: \"Sport\" (National Teams, Talent & Youth Sport), \"Leagues & Cup\" (organizing championships for various leagues and cup tournaments), \"Officiating\" (managing referees), and \"Education\" (initial and continuous training for Swiss ice hockey). The SIHF also engages in marketing and sponsorship activities, with partners like Denner, KPT, Swiss Life, and official broadcasters, which likely contribute to its funding.\n\n**Key Products/Services:**\nThe SIHF's core services include:\n*   **National Teams:** Managing men's, women's, and junior national teams (U20, U18, U17, U16, U14).\n*   **League and Cup Organization:** Organizing various championships, including the National League, Sky Swiss League, MyHockey League, PostFinance Women's League, junior leagues, and cup tournaments.\n*   **Youth and Talent Development:** Implementing programs like \"Foundation, Talent, Elite, Mastery\" and \"swissmadehockey\" guidelines for training junior players. It also includes initiatives like the Denner Swiss Ice Hockey Day and the Swiss Ice Hockey School Trophy.\n*   **Officiating:** Training and managing referees.\n*   **Education:** Providing initial and continuing education for the entire Swiss ice hockey community.\n*   **Events:** Hosting events like the Swiss Ice Hockey Night and awards ceremonies.\n\n**Market Position:**\nThe SIHF holds the exclusive position as the governing body of ice hockey in Switzerland, recognized by the IIHF. It oversees the entire structure of Swiss ice hockey, from grassroots youth development to professional leagues and national team representation on the international stage.\n\n**Headquarters Location:**\nThe headquarters of the Swiss Ice Hockey Federation is located at Flughofstrasse 50, CH-8152 Glattbrugg, Switzerland.\n\n**Recent News / Notable Achievements:**\n*   The SIHF was a founding member of the International Ice Hockey Federation in 1908.\n*   The men's national team achieved \"Silver Medallists 2025\" and \"Silver Heroes 2024\".\n*   The women's national team achieved \"Olympic Bronze Medallists 2026\".\n*   Youth coach Markus Graf developed the \"Foundation, Talent, Elite, Mastery\" program, which has been adopted as the SIHF's guiding principle. He also created \"swissmadehockey\" guidelines for training junior players, which influenced the training approach for the men's national team.\n\n**Challenges:**\nThe provided information does not explicitly detail any specific challenges faced by the Swiss Ice Hockey Federation.",
